# The game over screen's message sits on the title picture with nothing
# behind it (build 93a). GameOverScreen loads the font through
# DrawArtTiles2 (ps2.asm:12320), which clears colour 11 -- the whole of
# the window fill tile -- from every tile, so the fill cells the message
# is typed with are transparent. Up to build 93 the port placed the font
# as it was, and the message sat in a solid box of colour 11 ($800) that
# hid the middle planet. A level-1 Rolf against Mother Brain loses in a
# round.

start battle $103
party 1 1
limit 4000
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen gameover
wait ticks 400
shot 01_game_over
expect script $1218
expect pixel 82 82 $000
# (build 153) The background is GameOverScreen's own table (loc_6C5DA,
# ps2.asm:12284): the title's two rows up, and two rows of its own below.
# Up to 152 the port drew the title's: the middle planet's pixel was at
# 190,112 (black now), and the bottom two rows were the title's.
expect pixel 190 96 $260
expect pixel 190 112 $000
expect pixel 1 208 $420
